      "FlagConflict": {
        "description": "A two-value dispute the model raises instead of overwriting.\n\n``field`` names either a SCALAR field of the ``target`` entity (``company``,\n``end_date``, …) or — #218 — one of its BULLET LISTS (``responsibilities`` /\n``achievements``), in which case ``existing``/``incoming`` carry the two\ncontradicting bullet texts verbatim rather than field values. Both shapes\nland on the same ``Conflict`` channel; the applier attaches the resolved\nentity's id so the resolution endpoint can write back to that bullet.\n\nDeciding that two differently-worded bullets contradict is the reconciler\nmodel's judgement (ADR-062 clause 1) — no deterministic matcher may make it,\nwhich is why this is an op the model emits and not a post-pass.",
        "properties": {
          "op": {
            "const": "flag_conflict",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "target": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "field": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "existing": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "incoming": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "target",
          "field",
          "existing",
          "incoming"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "MatchExisting": {
        "description": "The reconciler's way to SAY \"already there\" (#707, ADR-046 amended\n2026-09-16) — model-emittable, writes nothing.\n\nThe new information names an entity the profile already holds under another\nsurface form — a translation (\"English\" for \"Englisch\"), a synonym, an\nabbreviation — and adds nothing new about it. Before this op the model's only\nchannel for that judgement was SILENCE, and the import witness\n(``reconcile/import_witness.py``) cannot tell silence from dropping: on a\nDE→EN second-source import it listed nearly every entry of the second CV as\n``no_op_carried_entry`` while the vault held every one of them (#707).\n\n``target`` is the existing entity's id (the profile view the model reads keeps\nids on EXISTING entries — ADR-078 strips them from the INCOMING block only);\n``incoming`` is the incoming entry's name exactly as the new information\nwrites it. Scope: the six flat sections, whose upsert ops carry no\n``target``; engagements keep rule 7's ``upsert_*(target=…)`` mechanism, and\na ``match_existing`` aimed at an engagement id records its receipt and\nrescues nothing at the witness.\n\nThe applier (``_apply_match_existing``) resolves ``target`` through\n``resolve_any``, records ONE :class:`applire.schemas.profile.MatchReceipt`\non ``ApplyResult.matched`` and mutates nothing. Never a ``set_field``: it\nfills nothing, overwrites nothing, creates no alias.",
        "properties": {
          "op": {
            "const": "match_existing",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "target": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "incoming": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "target",
          "incoming"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "RequestConfirmation": {
        "description": "A targeted question the reconciler asks instead of guessing (US185).\n\n**Two emitters, and only one of them may fill the localized half.** The\nmodel emits this op (prompt rule 6) with a plain ``question`` and plain\n``options`` in the session's language — that is its whole vocabulary. The\nnine DETERMINISTIC builders (``apply.py`` x8, ``attribution.py`` x1) fill\n``question_i18n`` / ``options_i18n`` / ``option_keys`` instead, and those\nthree fields are **stripped from raw model output before validation**\n(``engine._parse_ops``), so a hallucinated ``option_keys`` cannot exist.\n\nThat is ADR-063's own governing rule — *never widen an op the model can emit\nwith a more powerful parameter* — applied to the 2026-09-05 amendment. The\namendment's sketch said ``question``/``options`` \"become {de, en} payloads\";\nwritten that way the model would be filling a locale payload it cannot be\nheld to, and ``option_keys`` (the identity a vault WRITE resolves on) would\nbe model-supplied. The three decided clauses are unchanged: stable keys, a\nlanguage-independent persisted form, door parity.\n\n``options`` and ``options_i18n``/``option_keys`` are positionally paired\nwhen the localized half is present: index *i* of each names the same choice.",
        "properties": {
          "op": {
            "const": "request_confirmation",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "question": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "options": {
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "type": "array"
          },
          "context": {
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "type": "object"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "question",
          "options"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
